WEBVTT

00:05:28.699 --> 00:05:30.826
but this is a small neural circuit.

00:05:31.285 --> 00:05:33.287
Small enough that we can identify it

00:05:33.329 --> 00:05:35.998
and study it with the tools
that are available today.

00:05:37.166 --> 00:05:39.001
And this is what I'm trying to do.

00:05:39.794 --> 00:05:42.838
I have built a model of what I believe
is the neural circuit

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:45.424
that calculates how
the dragonfly should turn.

00:05:46.092 --> 00:05:47.676
And here is the cool result.

00:05:47.718 --> 00:05:49.345
In the model,

00:05:49.387 --> 00:05:54.100
dragonflies do coordinate transformations
in only one computational step,

00:05:54.141 --> 00:05:55.768
one layer of neurons.

00:05:56.394 --> 00:05:59.271
This is something
we can test and understand.